"en\":\"1823\",\"hi\":\"1823\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"1833\",\"hi\":\"1833\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1853\",\"hi\":\"1853\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Charter Act, 1833 (3 & 4 Will. 4 c. 85); M. Laxmikanth Indian Polity - Historical Background\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f56ae522-5743-47b0-89fd-d873979bb2ef\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What clearer functional distinction was introduced in the Governor-General's Council by the Charter Act of 1853?\",\"hi\":\"1853 के चार्टर एक्ट ने गवर्नर-जनरल की परिषद में किन कार्यों के बीच अधिक स्पष्ट कार्यात्मक भेद स्थापित किया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Legislative and executive functions\",\"hi\":\"विधायी और कार्यकारी कार्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Judiciary and armed forces\",\"hi\":\"न्यायपालिका और सशस्त्र बल\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Revenue and foreign trade only\",\"hi\":\"केवल राजस्व और विदेश व्यापार\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Crown and Parliament\",\"hi\":\"क्राउन और संसद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Charter Act, 1853 (16 & 17 Vict. c. 95); M. Laxmikanth Indian Polity - Historical Background\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f494eefb-b808-4b4f-b8df-6f4fe2850605\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which expression was used for the Company's Indian territories under Pitt's India Act of 1784?\",\"hi\":\"पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट, 1784 में कंपनी के भारतीय क्षेत्रों के लिए किस अभिव्यक्ति का प्रयोग किया गया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"British possessions in India\",\"hi\":\"भारत में ब्रिटिश अधिकार वाले क्षेत्र\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Indian federation\",\"hi\":\"भारतीय संघ\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Crown dominions of Asia\",\"hi\":\"एशिया के क्राउन डोमिनियन\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"United Provinces of India\",\"hi\":\"भारत के संयुक्त प्रांत\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Pitt's India Act, 1784 (24 Geo. 3 Sess. 2 c. 25); M. Laxmikanth Indian Polity - Historical Background\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f1e1ee83-31d3-4e81-a2a4-b1c21289c1e6\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How did the Charter Act of 1853 differ from earlier renewals regarding the duration of Company rule?\",\"hi\":\"कंपनी शासन की अवधि के संबंध में 1853 का चार्टर एक्ट पूर्व नवीनीकरणों से कैसे भिन्न था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It renewed rule for exactly ten years\",\"hi\":\"इसने ठीक दस वर्ष के लिए शासन नवीनीकृत किया\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It renewed rule for twenty years\",\"hi\":\"इसने बीस वर्ष के लिए शासन नवीनीकृत किया\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It continued rule until Parliament otherwise provided\",\"hi\":\"इसने संसद के अन्यथा प्रावधान करने तक शासन जारी रखा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It immediately ended Company rule\",\"hi\":\"इसने कंपनी शासन तत्काल समाप्त कर दिया\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Charter Act, 1853 (16 & 17 Vict. c. 95), section 1; M. Laxmikanth Indian Polity - Historical Background\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f0a808aa-ab6c-4a47-9e22-a64c504ea83a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Pitt's India Act reduced the number of ordinary members in the Governor-General's Council from four to how many?\",\"hi\":\"पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट ने गवर्नर-जनरल की परिषद के साधारण सदस्यों की संख्या चार से घटाकर कितनी कर दी?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Two\",\"hi\":\"दो\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Three\",\"hi\":\"तीन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Five\",\"hi\":\"पाँच\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Six\",\"hi\":\"छह\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Pitt's India Act, 1784 (24 Geo. 3 Sess. 2 c. 25); M. Laxmikanth Indian Polity - Historical Background\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ee695b4d-7228-4f01-97bc-af597b12dc85\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What did the Charter Act of 1813 expressly declare regarding sovereignty over the Company's Indian territories?\",\"hi\":\"1813 के चार्टर एक्ट ने कंपनी के भारतीय क्षेत्रों पर संप्रभुता के संबंध में क्या स्पष्ट घोषणा की?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The undoubted sovereignty of the British Crown\",\"hi\":\"ब्रिटिश क्राउन की निर्विवाद संप्रभुता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The sovereignty of the Court of Directors\",\"hi\":\"कोर्ट ऑफ डायरेक्टर्स की संप्रभुता\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Complete Indian federation\",\"hi\":\"पूर्ण भारतीय संघ\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"French sovereignty\",\"hi\":\"फ्रांसीसी संप्रभुता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Charter Act, 1813 (53 Geo. 3 c. 155); M. Laxmikanth Indian Polity - Historical Background\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ed856bbe-3965-42f0-b2e6-aeebbdbc8a41\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Who was made the Nawab of Bengal after the defeat of Sirajuddaulah?\",\"hi\":\"सिराजुद्दौला की पराजय के बाद बंगाल का नवाब किसे बनाया गया था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Shah Alam II\",\"hi\":\"शाह आलम द्वितीय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Shuja-ud-Daulah\",\"hi\":\"शुजाउद्दौला\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Mir Jafar\",\"hi\":\"मीर जाफर\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Muhammad Raza Khan\",\"hi\":\"मुहम्मद रजा खान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-19: National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/hess202.pdf#page=6 — Printed page 14, PDF page 6: Mir Jafar, Mir Qasim, Buxar, Diwani and use of Bengal revenues\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Our Pasts–III, Class VIII, Chapter 2: From Trade to Territory\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/hess202.pdf#page=6\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 14, PDF page 6: Mir Jafar, Mir Qasim, Buxar, Diwani and use of Bengal revenues\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Printed page 14, PDF page 6: Mir Jafar, Mir Qasim, Buxar, Diwani and use of Bengal revenues\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ecdbc6b3-61c3-496c-ac86-37eee10be7c0\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"After the transitional increase provided by the Charter Act of 1853 was completed, how many of the eighteen Company directors were Crown appointees?\",\"hi\":\"1853 के चार्टर एक्ट में निर्धारित संक्रमण पूरा होने के बाद अठारह कंपनी निदेशकों में से कितने क्राउन द्वारा नियुक्त होने थे?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Three\",\"hi\":\"तीन\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Four\",\"hi\":\"चार\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Six\",\"hi\":\"छह\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Nine\",\"hi\":\"नौ\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Based on: Charter Act, 1853 (16 & 17 Vict. c. 95), sections 3-6\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ec38cdc4-02bb-466b-b222-45c57af761f2\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Appeals from the Supreme Court at Calcutta were made to which authority in England?\",\"hi\":\"कलकत्ता के सुप्रीम कोर्ट से अपील इंग्लैंड में किस प्राधिकारी के पास की जाती थी?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"House of Commons alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल हाउस ऑफ कॉमन्स\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Court of Directors\",\"hi\":\"कोर्ट ऑफ डायरेक्टर्स\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Treasury Board\",\"hi\":\"ट्रेजरी बोर्ड\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"King-in-Council\",\"hi\":\"किंग-इन-काउंसिल\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-19: Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) — https://www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/ebooks/XI_U3_Legal_Studies.pdf — Printed pp. 141–143: Regulating Act, Governor-General and council, Section 13, Letters Patent, Supreme Court composition, jurisdiction and defects; National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS) — https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/315en/315_History_Eng_Lesson16.pdf — Sections 16.6–16.7, printed pp. 10 and 12: first parliamentary control measure, unified administration, Warren Hastings and Supreme Court at Calcutta\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Legal Studies, Class XI, Unit 3: Historical Evolution of the Indian Legal System\",\"institution\":\"Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE)\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbse.gov.in/cbsenew/ebooks/XI_U3_Legal_Studies.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 141–143: Regulating Act, Governor-General and council, Section 13, Letters Patent, Supreme Court composition, jurisdiction and defects\"},{\"title\":\"History (315), Lesson 16: Establishment of British Rule in India till 1857\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/315en/315_History_Eng_Lesson16.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Sections 16.6–16.7, printed pp. 10 and 12: first parliamentary control measure, unified administration, Warren Hastings and Supreme Court at Calcutta\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Printed pp. 141–143: Regulating Act, Governor-General and council, Section 13, Letters Patent, Supreme Court composition, jurisdiction and defects; Sections 16.6–16.7, printed pp. 10 and 12: first parliamentary control measure, unified administration, Warren Hastings and Supreme Court at Calcutta\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ec20c380-fdf4-46ae-9e6c-738f2f19ee75